<tr>
<td><strong><code>THE-COMPLETE-GUIDE.md</code></strong></td>
<td style="text-align: right;">551</td>
<td><strong>Everything gathered across five separate searches, in one document.</strong> Sound design, music production, audio engineering, music technology, music business. The single most complete written thing here.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>PRIVATE-SCHOOLS.md</code></strong></td>
<td style="text-align: right;">461</td>
<td><strong>114 private institutions</strong> in Spain, Portugal, Netherlands and Italy, searched in English <em>and</em> Spanish, Portuguese, Dutch and Italian. This is where most of the fake-master's traps were caught.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>DEGREE-CHECK.md</code></strong></td>
<td style="text-align: right;">388</td>
<td><strong>The certificate audit.</strong> All 1,091 records re-checked against what they actually award. This is what <em>"I want masters not a certificate"</em> produced — <em>título propio</em>, RNCP level-5 <em>Mastère</em>, <em>pós-graduação</em>, UK validation chains.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>PATHS-DEEP-DIVE.md</code></strong></td>
<td style="text-align: right;">336</td>
<td><strong>The three doors explained in depth</strong>, written when you were deciding between them, plus the section explaining what a "portfolio" actually means in practice.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>EUROPE-GAPFILL.md</code></strong></td>
<td style="text-align: right;">329</td>
<td><strong>85 institutions across 26 countries that no earlier sweep had touched.</strong> The pass that existed to make sure nothing in Europe was missed.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>DOOR3.md</code></strong></td>
<td style="text-align: right;">260</td>
