<hr />
<h1>6 · How the research was made</h1>
<p><code>.masters-search/</code> — the toolchain. Open these only to re-run or extend the search.</p>
<h3>The two files that do the real thinking</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>File</th>
<th>What it is</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>qual_level.py</code></strong></td>
<td><strong>Separates real master's degrees from certificates.</strong> Handles negation, so <em>"a genuine second-cycle degree, </em><em>not</em><em> a Lehrgang"</em> reads correctly instead of backwards. Knows <em>máster propio</em>, <em>título propio</em>, <em>Diploma Accademico di II livello</em> vs <em>Master di I livello</em>, RNCP levels, <em>Universitätslehrgang</em>.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>corrections.py</code></strong></td>
<td><strong>Lets a verifier's correction override a stale field.</strong> 75 of 127 verified Door-3 records say a machine field is wrong. This catches the dangerous ones — the Babelsberg and FAMU <strong>live piano auditions</strong> hiding behind "Exam/interview only", Edinburgh's <em>under €1.5k</em> that is really <strong>£29,900</strong>.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
