<hr />
<h1>Two things worth knowing about all of this</h1>
<p><strong>"Never checked" is not "fine".</strong> 249 of the 398 Door-3 records were never read by a second agent. In the app that state has no colour of its own — it is an empty meter slot — precisely so it can never be mistaken for good news.</p>
<p><strong>A correction outranks a field.</strong> Where a verifier's prose contradicts a structured value, the prose wins and you get shown the sentence. Edinburgh's recorded band says <em>under €1.5k/yr</em>; the real figure is <strong>≈£29,900</strong>. KASK's says the same; it is <strong>≈€8,800</strong>. Both render struck through and marked wrong, and neither can reach a "cheap" filter.</p></body></html>